m-organized Wall Lighting branch and was kept in full per Rule 0 (product type = lighting fixture, room word does not exclude). Excluded as exact-same-listing / non-canonical duplicates (verified via urlResolver redirect / dead-link check): /us/c/wall/undercabinet and /us/c/wall/undercabinet-lighting-broken both resolve (urlResolver) to the same relative_url as /us/c/wall/undercabinet-lighting (kept, 44); /us/c/wall/sconces does not resolve at all (urlResolver returns null -- dead/orphaned category, superseded by Wall > Decorative Wall which is kept). /us/c/outdoor/gas-lanterns/ceiling returns 0 products (empty placeholder, robots=noindex) and was dropped. Excluded as lighting parts/hardware, not fixtures (wiring-hardware exclusion): /us/c/ceiling/accessories (2 SKUs, sample titles 'Dyna Mechanical Connector', 'Five Light Multiport Canopy' -- mounting hardware); /us/c/shades (14 SKUs, all fabric lamp/sconce replacement shades, e.g. 'Schumacher 16in Empire Shade' -- lighting parts not standalone fixtures). Excluded the entire /architectural/ microsite (11 sub-lines: recessed-downlights, cylinders, led-strips-and-channels, brox-linear-led, low-voltage-pendants, low-voltage-heads, freejack-canopies, monorail-track-lighting, wall-monorail, kable-lite, landscape; 513 products total, counts individually verified via GraphQL e.g. recessed-downlights=40, monorail-track-lighting=96, kable-lite=53) as a mixed roll-up per the 'drop, don't pad' rule: sampled item titles across the largest sub-lines (freejack-canopies, led-strips-and-channels, low-voltage-heads, kable-lite, wall-monorail) show they are overwhelmingly transformers, mounting clips/tape, canopies, and lens/shield parts for a professional low-voltage track system (e.g. 'Kable Lite Remote Transformer-600W Mag 12v', 'Channel Mounting Double Sided Tape 095', 'Wall MonoRail End Power Feed'), with only a minority of true fixtures (e.g. 'FreeJack Melrose II Pendant') mixed in and no clean way to separate fixtures from hardware at category granularity. Confirmed architectural/landscape (81 items) is NOT a duplicate of the kept outdoor/landscape (12 items, consumer landscape lighting) -- clearly different product counts/catalogs (professional systems division vs consumer). Excluded as facet/certification filters, not distinct product types (site's own cross-cutting tag categories spanning every fixture type already counted): /us/c/dark-sky (Dark Sky compliant), /us/c/wet-damp-rated, /us/c/ada (ADA compliant), /us/c/back-in-stock. Excluded per NEVER EXTRACT rules: /us/c/fans + /us/c/smart-fans (ceiling fans, explicitly out of scope), /us/c/bulbs, /us/c/new-introductions, /us/c/best-sellers/*, /us/c/sale/*, /us/c/dallas-market-specials/*, /us/c/market-specials, /us/c/shop/* and /us/c/shop-all (all thematic/promo/lookbook pages), /us/c/edit/* (curated style lists), /us/c/our-designers* and /us/c/our-collections/* (designer- and brand-line listing/rollup pages -- facet re-cuts of the same catalog by designer/collection brand, not distinct product types), /us/c/paper-templates (installation aid, not a product), /us/c/stonestrong (thin/noindex placeholder page, no visible product grid). No duplicate-company flag: this is the primary visualcomfort.com US storefront for Visual Comfort & Co., a single company.",
